 "SEC-HC-09": {
  "ok": false,
  "key_votes": 3,
  "picks": "DDD",
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "distractor_quality": "strong",
  "why": [
   "second defensible: Ambiguous stem. D is the only option with no mechanical fault, but it makes the whose-clause restrictive on an already-definite 'The strait's array'. A has the natural nonrestrictive commas and fails only on 'array of turbines produce' -- notional plural agreement with 'an array of' is widely attested (like 'a number of') and many editors would pass it. The category label ('nonrestrictive addition, with agreement') suggests A may even be the intended key. Either way two options survive; needs a rewrite so that the commas and the verb agree in one option."
  ]
 },
